--- body ---
## Context
`erg version` currently spot-checks a few known paths for other erg binaries
(e.g. tickets/erg). This misses binaries installed elsewhere in the project
tree. Walking the project directory finds all copies, so users see the full
picture: which are current, which are stale, which are obsolete.

## Actions
1. In `cmdVersion`, after reporting the running binary, walk the project root
   (or the tickets dir) with `filepath.WalkDir`, collecting any file named
   `erg` that is executable.
2. For each found binary, report path, hash, build date, and obsolescence
   status (same as the current spot-check logic).
3. Deduplicate the running binary itself from the walk results.

## Test
Place two `erg` binaries at different paths in a temp dir. Run `erg version`.
Both must appear in the output.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `erg version` lists all `erg` executables found under the project root
- [ ] Running binary is not double-reported
- [ ] Output format consistent with existing version output
- [ ] `make test` passes
